---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config';
import { organizationLd } from '../lib/jsonld';
---
<Base
  title="Privacy notice — Grovetrace"
  description="What Grovetrace collects when you book a demo, why, who processes it, how long it is kept, and how to have it deleted."
  jsonLd={[organizationLd()]}
>
  <section class="privacy">
    <div class="wrap inner prose">
      <h1>Privacy notice</h1>
      <p class="updated">Last updated 22 August 2026</p>

      <p>
        Grovetrace sells software for EU regulatory compliance, so it would be a
        poor look to be vague here. This page says exactly what happens to your
        data. It is short because very little happens to it.
      </p>

      <h2>What this site collects</h2>
      <p>
        Browsing grovetrace.com collects <strong>nothing</strong>. There is no
        analytics, no advertising pixel, no cookie banner, because there are no
        cookies to consent to. Fonts are served from this domain rather than a
        third-party CDN, so no request for them leaves for another company.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you fill in the demo form, it collects what you type: your name, work
        email, company, role, the commodities you selected, and — if you choose
        to answer — your approximate volume and the open question in your supply
        chain.
      </p>

      <h2>Why</h2>
      <p>
        To reply to you and to hold a useful first call. That is the only
        purpose. The lawful basis is your consent, given by submitting the form,
        and steps taken at your request before entering a contract.
      </p>
      <p>
        You will not be added to a mailing list, and your details are never sold,
        rented or shared for anyone else's marketing.
      </p>

      <h2>Who else processes it</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Web3Forms</strong> receives the form submission and forwards it
          to us by email. It is the delivery mechanism and does not retain your
          answers for its own purposes.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Cal.com</strong> handles the booking, if you go on to pick a
          time. Its script loads <em>only after</em> you submit the form — a
          visitor who never books never receives it.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Google Workspace</strong> hosts the mailbox the enquiry lands
          in, and the calendar invitation.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>How long it is kept</h2>
      <p>
        Enquiries are kept for <strong>24 months</strong> and then deleted. If a
        conversation becomes a customer relationship, the records that belong to
        that contract are kept for as long as the contract and applicable
        accounting law require.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        Under the GDPR you can ask for a copy of what is held about you, ask for
        it to be corrected or erased, object to its processing, or withdraw
        consent. Email <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a> and it
        will be actioned — deletion within 30 days, usually the same week. You
        may also complain to your national data protection authority.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Grovetrace — <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.
        For anything about this notice, use the same address.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .privacy { padding: 56px 0 72px; }
  .inner { max-width: 68ch; }
  h1 { font-size: clamp(1.9rem, 4vw, 2.5rem); margin-bottom: 6px; }
  .updated { color: var(--muted-foreground); font-size: 0.9rem; margin-bottom: 28px; }
  h2 { font-size: 1.2rem; margin: 32px 0 10px; }
  .prose p, .prose li { color: var(--muted-foreground); }
  .prose p + p { margin-top: 12px; }
  .prose strong { color: var(--foreground); }
  ul { padding-left: 1.1rem; display: grid; gap: 8px; margin-top: 8px; }
</style>
